.TH FERRIPRINT 1 "October 2026" "Ferriprint" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferriprint \- secure driverless IPP frontend for an existing native CUPS queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferriprint
.RB [ --config " PATH"]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ferriprint validates standard IPP media, margins, quality, tray, color and sides
against an operator-supplied private PPD and one managed profile per printer.
It forwards documents and resolved native options to an existing CUPS queue.
It does not rasterize documents, install vendor drivers, configure CUPS queues
or certify physical output.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default bootstrap file is ferriprint.toml in the current directory.
The packaged service reads /etc/ferriprint/ferriprint.toml.
Static printer identity, PPD and upstream paths belong in that file.
Editable mapping/default data belongs only in
.I state_dir/profiles/NAME.toml
and is validated against the PPD. See the installed TOML examples and setup guide.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Validate bootstrap configuration, private PPD and managed profiles offline.
No printer is contacted and no job is submitted.
.TP
.B serve
Start the frontend, probe upstream formats and reconcile durable jobs.
This is the default command when no subcommand is given.
.TP
.B setup
Create reviewed bootstrap configuration and a managed profile from an existing
CUPS queue and an operator-provided PPD. Consult
.B ferriprint setup --help
for required paths and mapping choices. This does not configure CUPS or print.
.TP
.B user password-hash
Generate an Argon2id password hash from protected standard input or a terminal.
Consult command help for the output file option. Never pass plaintext credentials
in command-line arguments or store them in public configuration.
.TP
.B abandon
Offline escape hatch for a job with unknown upstream submission outcome.
Requires explicit acknowledgement; the real upstream job may still print.
It releases local admission capacity but retains the audit record.
.SH SECURITY
Non-loopback listeners require TLS and explicit client networks.
Discovery visibility never grants access and TLS verification is not disabled.
The configured canonical FQDN must match its certificate.
Authenticated users own their jobs. An IPP requesting-user-name is not a credential.
Explicit anonymous trusted-LAN admission is a shared principal, not per-user isolation.
Administration always requires an authenticated admin role, including when anonymous
IPP printing is enabled. State-changing browser actions require a same-origin
CSRF-protected request.
.PP
Within the existing network/TLS boundary, unauthenticated capability
Get-Printer-Attributes and the corresponding-source offer are permitted.
All job operations, including Validate-Job, and web/job APIs still require a
verified user or an explicitly admitted shared anonymous source.
Invalid supplied credentials always fail, even on those read-only exceptions.
Printer authentication attributes reflect the request source so an existing
anonymous client is not silently forced to authenticate.
.PP
Private keys, password hashes, vendor PPDs and durable job state remain outside
public source/package archives. The service obtains TLS keys through systemd
LoadCredential from operator-managed root-only paths. Never broaden ACME key permissions.
.PP
Password hashes must be regular, non-symlink files effectively private to root
and the service UID. Keep originals root0600. A Linux systemd runtime file may
be root0440 with a named service-UID read ACL and no effective group/other access;
the ACL mask is not itself a group grant. No credential-path exemption is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ferriprint/ferriprint.toml
Operator-managed static bootstrap configuration; not supplied as an active conffile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/ferriprint
Private durable jobs, spool and managed profiles; retain across upgrades/removal.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ferriprint
Examples, setup/security/deployment guides, license notices and build metadata.
.SH INSTALLATION
The package does not enable, start or restart the service, import credentials, create a
queue or submit a print. Configure and check first, then explicitly start the
service after reviewing TLS, network admission, ownership and existing jobs.
Package removal refuses to stop an active frontend automatically: gracefully stop
it after checking jobs. Configuration, state and the service account are retained.
.SH SOURCE
The running service exposes the matching AGPL project source archive at /source.
Dependencies are fetched from the committed Cargo.lock; it is not a vendored
or offline dependency source bundle. Release assets include source, SPDX inventory,
checksums and a pinned-input build manifest, not a byte-reproducibility claim.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ipptool (1),
.BR lpstat (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
